{"id":"VHH__geo__delete_components_by_volume","collection":"VHH","category":"geo","source_path":"VHH/geo/delete_components_by_volume.json","root_names":["VHH::Core::Geometry::delete_components_by_volume"],"counts":{"nodes":33,"connections":62,"values":27,"overloads":1},"documentation_summary":"This compound deletes faces (by default) or points based on whether those points are inside an object. It will also generate scatter weights for that object to exclude the culled components. Because it's interanlly based on a volume, you are able to erode/grow the volume.","documentation_search":"delete components by volume This compound deletes faces (by default) or points based on whether those points are inside an object. It will also generate scatter weights for that object to exclude the culled components. Because it's interanlly based on a volume, you are able to erode/grow the volume. Input object to delete from The object you wish to cull from . culling object The object inside which the components are culled. points When this is true, the compound will delete points from the object to delete from rather than faces. volume mode Solid mode voxelizes the mesh with a solid interior. Shell mode voxelizes the mesh as a thickened surface with a hollow interior. volume resolution The resolution of the interior volume. Smaller numbers will cull \"tighter\" to the culling object. offset volume Erode/Expand the interior volume. adjust culling An fCurve that controls the erode/expand of the internal volume. Output culled object The resulting object. scatter weights Scatter weights array containing 0 (no poins) and 1 (all points).","port_names":["adjust_culling","culled_object","culling_object","object_to_delete_from","offset_volume","points","scatter_weights","volume_mode","volume_resolution"],"node_types_search":["Core::Array::find_all_true_in_array","Core::Array::flatten_nested_array","Core::Array::get_from_array","Core::Array::resize_array","Core::Array::sequence_array","Core: